meta {
  name: Cache Behaviour
  seq: 6
}

docs {
  Run these three requests **in order** to observe the in-memory response cache.

  The cache key is derived from the full request - endpoint, location, units and
  language - so changing any single parameter produces a different key and a
  fresh upstream call. Entries live for one hour.

  Watch the API logs while running. Each miss logs
  `Cache miss - fetching fresh weather data for {CacheKey}`; a hit logs nothing
  and returns without an upstream call.

  The response-time assertions are indicative, not exact: they assume a cold
  cache and a reachable OpenWeatherMap API. If request 1 fails its timing
  assertion, the entry was probably already cached from an earlier run - wait
  out the hour TTL or change `cityName`.
}
